<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-29T20:51:51+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:51:51 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[In 2021, billionaire Orlando Bravo paid $39.25 million for Phil Collins’s 1929 Miami Beach mansion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134569131.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Orlando Bravo has received approval to tear down a historic estate in Miami Beach that was once the home of Phil Collins. This demolition paves the way for a new luxury mansion, purposefully designed to combat flooding. The choice has ignited discussions about the importance of preserving historical sites in South Florida, with many advocates worried about the potential loss of early 20th-century architecture as climate challenges mount.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2021-billionaire-orlando-bravo-paid-39-25-million-for-phil-collinss-1929-miami-beach-mansion-months-later-he-won-approval-to-demolish-it-for-a-flood-resilient-home-with-tropical-gardens/articleshow/134569131.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2021-billionaire-orlando-bravo-paid-39-25-million-for-phil-collinss-1929-miami-beach-mansion-months-later-he-won-approval-to-demolish-it-for-a-flood-resilient-home-with-tropical-gardens/articleshow/134569131.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T20:34:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134569601,imgsize-2430118.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Punjabi man stabbed to death in Canada after intervening in racist altercation; sister alleges police delay]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134569421.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/punjabi-man-stabbed-to-death-in-canada-after-intervening-in-racist-altercation-sister-alleges-police-delay/articleshow/134569421.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/punjabi-man-stabbed-to-death-in-canada-after-intervening-in-racist-altercation-sister-alleges-police-delay/articleshow/134569421.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T20:27:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134569502,imgsize-796347.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Zhang Zhanshuo: The 19-year-old China swimmer who won record 7 Asian Games golds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134569209.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Zhang Zhanshuo, a young prodigy in the world of swimming, made an unforgettable mark at the 2026 Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya by clinching an astounding seven gold medals. He dominated the men's freestyle events, triumphing in the 200m, 400m, 800m, and 1,500m, alongside three relay victories. His exceptional performance not only set a new Asian Games record but also matched the highest number of individual golds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-zhang-zhanshuo-the-19-year-old-who-won-seven-golds-at-the-asian-games-from-a-kid-who-couldnt-swim-to-a-chinese-swimming-star/articleshow/134569209.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-zhang-zhanshuo-the-19-year-old-who-won-seven-golds-at-the-asian-games-from-a-kid-who-couldnt-swim-to-a-chinese-swimming-star/articleshow/134569209.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T20:05:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134569294,imgsize-904436.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1979, Ted Turner bought a 4,680-acre South Carolina barrier island to prevent development]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134568650.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ted Turner sold St Phillips Island to the South Carolina government for $4.9 million, much lower than its appraised value. The island will become part of South Carolina's state park system, focusing on ecosystem protection. Public access will be limited, allowing for educational programs and eco-tourism opportunities. Turner initially acquired the island in 1979 to prevent commercial development and has maintained its natural state.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1979-ted-turner-bought-a-4680-acre-south-carolina-barrier-island-to-prevent-development-38-years-later-he-sold-it-to-the-state-for-4-9-million-about-one-third-of-its-appraised-value-and-it-became-state-parkland/articleshow/134568650.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1979-ted-turner-bought-a-4680-acre-south-carolina-barrier-island-to-prevent-development-38-years-later-he-sold-it-to-the-state-for-4-9-million-about-one-third-of-its-appraised-value-and-it-became-state-parkland/articleshow/134568650.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T19:42:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134569095,imgsize-2449848.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Riverside twins whose wildfire-inspired hydrogel kept hot material from reigniting 9x longer than water]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134568674.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-henry-and-jack-grover-the-riverside-twins-whose-wildfire-inspired-hydrogel-kept-hot-material-from-reigniting-nine-times-longer-than-water/articleshow/134568674.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-henry-and-jack-grover-the-riverside-twins-whose-wildfire-inspired-hydrogel-kept-hot-material-from-reigniting-nine-times-longer-than-water/articleshow/134568674.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T20:04:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134568721,imgsize-106116.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Maria Menounos’ Encino home, after 21 years of renovations, lists for $6.995 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-