right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134564937.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/julia-child-lived-in-this-1889-cambridge-home-for-40-years-and-filmed-tv-shows-there-its-current-owners-paid-3-7-million-in-2009-renovated-it-and-have-now-listed-it-for-6-475-million/articleshow/134564937.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/julia-child-lived-in-this-1889-cambridge-home-for-40-years-and-filmed-tv-shows-there-its-current-owners-paid-3-7-million-in-2009-renovated-it-and-have-now-listed-it-for-6-475-million/articleshow/134564937.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T18:57:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134565010,imgsize-118760.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2023, Texas mogul paid $36 million for 11,000-sq-ft home; months later, the house was demolished]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134567682.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Texas property developer recently demolished the Wood Residence, a historic mansion in Coral Gables, Florida. The estate, designed by Alfred Browning Parker, was not designated as a historic landmark. Local preservation advocates expressed frustration over regulatory loopholes allowing such demolitions without public hearings. The demolition reflects a broader trend driven by rising land values in South Florida’s luxury real estate market.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2023-texas-mogul-felix-sorkin-paid-36-million-for-an-11000-sq-ft-coral-gables-home-designed-by-alfred-browning-parker-months-later-the-1963-modernist-house-was-demolished-for-a-replacement/articleshow/134567682.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2023-texas-mogul-felix-sorkin-paid-36-million-for-an-11000-sq-ft-coral-gables-home-designed-by-alfred-browning-parker-months-later-the-1963-modernist-house-was-demolished-for-a-replacement/articleshow/134567682.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T18:41:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134567951,imgsize-1286423.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin sixth-grader trains machine-learning model to spot lithium deposits with 89% accuracy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134564891.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ishaan Dokania, a sixth-grader from Oregon, is exploring lithium resource identification using satellite imagery and machine learning. His project reached 89% accuracy in predicting potential lithium deposits after addressing data noise and testing various algorithms. Ishaan's innovative approach combines geology and remote sensing to streamline mineral exploration. He is competing as a finalist in the 2026 Thermo Fisher Scientific Junior Innovators Challenge.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-ishaan-dokania-the-indian-origin-beaverton-sixth-grader-who-trained-a-machine-learning-model-on-satellite-data-to-spot-potential-lithium-deposits-with-89-accuracy/articleshow/134564891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-ishaan-dokania-the-indian-origin-beaverton-sixth-grader-who-trained-a-machine-learning-model-on-satellite-data-to-spot-potential-lithium-deposits-with-89-accuracy/articleshow/134564891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T18:56:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://