hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134559274.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A nearly 5-acre Bridgehampton estate featuring a replica 15th-century Buddhist temple has been listed for $7.5 million. Manhattan doctor and entrepreneur Roshini Raj bought the property for $3.95 million in 2022 and later made extensive changes. The estate includes a large main house, gardens, koi ponds, a pool, orchards and several leisure spaces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2022-manhattan-doctor-roshini-raj-paid-3-95-million-for-a-nearly-5-acre-bridgehampton-estate-with-a-replica-15th-century-buddhist-temple-after-3-million-in-updates-she-is-asking-7-5-million/articleshow/134559274.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2022-manhattan-doctor-roshini-raj-paid-3-95-million-for-a-nearly-5-acre-bridgehampton-estate-with-a-replica-15th-century-buddhist-temple-after-3-million-in-updates-she-is-asking-7-5-million/articleshow/134559274.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T17:50:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134559469,imgsize-113166.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An Essex family set aside its entire farm roughly 30 years ago; after farming resumed in 2014]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134564957.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Braxted Park Estate has initiated a 200-acre biodiversity recovery project following ten years of observation on 50 acres. This approach aims to enhance local ecological conditions and meet developers' biodiversity obligations. Property developers can purchase biodiversity units through the estate's habitat bank to comply with legal requirements. A long-term management agreement ensures the land will be protected and monitored for 30 years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/an-essex-family-set-aside-its-entire-farm-roughly-30-years-ago-after-farming-resumed-in-2014-50-acres-stayed-wild-regenerated-with-oak-and-scrub-and-helped-inspire-a-200-acre-nature-recovery-plan/articleshow/134564957.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/an-essex-family-set-aside-its-entire-farm-roughly-30-years-ago-after-farming-resumed-in-2014-50-acres-stayed-wild-regenerated-with-oak-and-scrub-and-helped-inspire-a-200-acre-nature-recovery-plan/articleshow/134564957.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T17:43:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134565788,imgsize-1143823.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Anna Luísa Beserra, a Brazilian scientist whose teenage idea turned dirty water into drinking water using just sunlight]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134562515.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Anna Luisa Beserra established Safe Drinking Water for All to focus on creating affordable sanitation and water solutions. Among her innovations is Aqualuz, a system harnessing sunlight to purify rainwater, benefiting over 10,000 individuals. She also developed Aquasalina, Aquafilter, and Aquatorre to serve diverse community requirements, while training local technicians for sustainable practices.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-anna-lusa-beserra-a-brazilian-scientist-whose-teenage-idea-turned-dirty-water-into-drinking-water-using-just-sunlight/articleshow/134562515.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-anna-lusa-beserra-a-brazilian-scientist-whose-teenage-idea-turned-dirty-water-into-drinking-water-using-just-sunlight/articleshow/134562515.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134562541,imgsize-771530.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado rancher wins wind project after $50,000 fight over oil drilling on his land]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134559004.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Colorado rancher spent $50,000 fighting oil drilling on his 7,000-acre property after companies used his land to reach neighbouring mineral reserves. Nearly a decade later, Weld County commissioners approved a wind project on part of his ranch. The rancher says the project could provide income to help his daughters continue the family’s cattle business.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-rancher-spent-50000-fighting-oil-infrastructure-he-did-not-want-on-his-7000-acre-ranch-after-nearly-a-decade-officials-approved-a-wind-project-that-lets-his-family-finally-earn-from-energy-on-its-own-land/articleshow/134559004.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-rancher-spent-50000-fighting-oil-infrastructure-he-did-not-want-on-his-7000-acre-ranch-after-nearly-a-decade-officials-approved-a-wind-project-that-lets-his-family-finally-earn-from-energy-on-its-own-land/articleshow/134559004.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134559222,imgsize-139498.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[18-year-old Washington student wins Doodle for Google with $55K scholarship]]></title><des